meta {
  name: Post GPS batch (sim boat)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/gps
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  DeviceId: AA:BB:CC:DD:99:01
  Stream-Id: sim:test-run
}

body:json {
  {
    "points": [
      { "lat": 39.92, "lon": 9.65, "speed": 13.5, "course": 180.0, "altitude": 5, "sats": 9, "timestamp": "2026-11-05T09:00:00.000Z" },
      { "lat": 39.92005, "lon": 9.65, "speed": 13.5, "course": 180.0, "altitude": 5, "sats": 9, "timestamp": "2026-11-05T09:00:01.000Z" }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Todo 66: the sandbox player posts its tape in windows (one round trip per window
  instead of one per fix, ~415 ms each). Same rules as POST /gps: DeviceId header,
  numeric lat/lon, `simulated` is forced on, the device row is upserted once and the
  whole window is one batched INSERT. 1..500 fixes; each keeps its own timestamp,
  which is the TAPE's epoch - that is what keeps a compressed race recording race
  time instead of wall time. Answers {status, stored, simulated, persisted, batch}.
}
